# P2P group owner only: does it satisfy the Wireless debugging gate? 2026-11-27.
# Curated transcript. The STA was removed first so nothing else could satisfy the
# gate; the phone hotspot was off. The probe held a group owner for 240 s.

# 1. The GO is up with an address, a channel and a role, but there is no STA.
$ nmcli connection down phonelink          # laptop AP off: no STA, no hotspot
$ adb shell settings get global adb_wifi_enabled
0
$ adb shell am start -n org.phonelink.p2pprobe/.MainActivity --ei hold 240000
$ adb shell dumpsys wifip2p | grep "CURRENTLY OPEN"
netId=0, startTime=11-27 20:12:29.554, channelFrequency=6055, groupRole=GroupOwner, numConnectedClients=0, numCumulativeClients=0, sessionDurationMillis=0, idleDurationMillis=0 CURRENTLY OPEN EVENT
$ adb shell ip -4 -o addr show p2p-p2p0-0
43: p2p-p2p0-0    inet 192.168.49.1/24 brd 192.168.49.255 scope global p2p-p2p0-0
$ adb shell cmd wifi status | head -1
Wifi is enabled                            # no "connected to", no SSID/BSSID

# 2. Writing the toggle is refused: with no client association `WifiInfo`
#    has Net ID -1, so AdbDebuggingManager's getCurrentWifiApInfo() returns null.
$ adb shell settings put global adb_wifi_enabled 1
$ adb shell settings get global adb_wifi_enabled
0
11-27 20:12:30.549  1596  1615 I AdbDebuggingManager: Not connected to any wireless network. Not enabling adbwifi.

# 3. Keeper tries as well and loses; the platform reverts its write at once.
11-27 20:12:31.059  2742  2742 I WifiDebug: enabled wireless debugging
11-27 20:12:31.061  1596  1615 I AdbDebuggingManager: Not connected to any wireless network. Not enabling adbwifi.

# 4. 5555 is unaffected: it was pinned earlier in the boot and stays on the
#    wildcard address, with the toggle at 0 and only a GO for a link.
$ adb shell getprop service.adb.tcp.port
5555

# 5. The GO and a STA did coexist long enough to satisfy the gate, and the
#    toggle flipped to 1 (satisfied by the STA, not the GO). The coexistence
#    was short-lived: at 20:16:29 wlan0 had no address, the toggle was 0 again,
#    and the laptop AP had to be restarted.
$ nmcli connection up phonelink
$ adb shell settings get global adb_wifi_enabled
1
$ adb shell ip -4 -o addr show wlan0
36: wlan0    inet 192.168.77.232/24 brd 192.168.77.255 scope global dynamic wlan0
$ adb shell dumpsys wifip2p | grep -m1 "CURRENTLY OPEN"
netId=0, ... channelFrequency=6055, groupRole=GroupOwner, numConnectedClients=0 ... CURRENTLY OPEN EVENT
$ adb shell ip -4 -o addr show wlan0        # 20:16:29, after the 240 s hold
(none)
$ adb shell settings get global adb_wifi_enabled
0
$ adb shell getprop service.adb.tcp.port
5555

# Summary: the toggle is STA-only. A GO with an address, a role and DHCP is not
# enough, and neither is Keeper writing the setting. STA + GO coexistence is
# not a stable link on this phone.
